Task: Verify schema and access (Phase 1, Tier 1)

WHAT CHANGED
Extended scripts/verify-account-deletion.ts to stage a rental statement
(file D) in the `property-files` bucket, uploaded by the co-owner GUEST into
the OWNER's property, backed by a real rental_payments row. Added five checks
covering it. Added scripts/verify-rental-payment-rls.sql, a reusable RLS proof
for the new columns.

Files:
  scripts/verify-account-deletion.ts (modified)
  scripts/verify-rental-payment-rls.sql (new)

THE CORE WHY
The harness passed before this change while providing ZERO coverage of
statement_path — it staged only `invoices` files and never touched
rental_payments. A green harness that does not exercise the new column is
worse than no coverage, because it reads as proof. File D deliberately uses a
different bucket AND a different table from the existing fixtures, so it
exercises a genuinely separate branch of both functions.

RLS applies per ROW, not per column, so migration 062's policies should cover
063's columns automatically. "Should" is not evidence, and workflow.md requires
proving a non-owner is DENIED rather than only that the owner is allowed. The
SQL proof runs as the `authenticated` role with a JWT claim, which is how
PostgREST reaches these policies — as superuser RLS is bypassed and every check
would pass vacuously.

